-- title:
--   A linearized small-prime zeta correction estimate
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be finite with $m=|\kappa|$, let $R>1$, $w\ge2$ be integers, and let $T\ge0$. Suppose $t,u\in\mathbb R^\kappa$ have every coordinate bounded in absolute value by $T$. Set $B=B(R,w,T)$ and assume
--   $$
--   B\le1,\qquad48m(w+1)B^2\le1.
--   $$
--   Then the normalized small-prime correction satisfies
--   $$
--   \|Z^{\mathrm{small}}_{R,w}(t,u)-1\|\le96m(w+1)B^2.
--   $$
--   The hypotheses and conclusion use the same phase-magnitude scale.
